      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When I mention \"cultural clashes\" in the workforce context of those regions, I am referring to the deep-seated tribalism and ethnic divisions that are often present. These aren't just minor disagreements; they are fundamental societal fault lines that can easily spill over into the workplace. In many parts of Southeast Asia and Sub-Saharan Africa, loyalty to one's immediate ethnic or tribal group often supersedes loyalty to the company. Therefore, maintaining a unified culture requires far more complex, localized management than simply implementing standard HR policies.",
      "source": "target",
